Z||000000||Jaei Sun||01-22-2001||07:09 PM||||On my 87 GT, where the passenger side headlight flap is mounted to the hood there is some pretty bad cracking.  When ever the headlight goes up the crack is opened up.  Needless to say after I saw this problem I stopped using the headlights completely.<P>Now my question is how should I go about fixing this?  I saw some previous posts saying to use a few methods:<BR>1.  a product called FMC<BR>2.  3M hard plastic repair kit<BR>3.  epoxy / fiberglass cloth (fiberglassin')<BR>4.  a product called SMC (fiberglass resin/thin body filler)<BR>5.  3M Polyester body filler # 8101 (I guess the service man. said to use this)<P>Now I want a fix that is really strong and rigid (since there is a lot of pressure put on this area by the spring on the flap. And to me right now time is no issue but money is that is why I just don't get a whole new hood.<P>Should I use any of those listed above or does anyone know of anything better?  Any suggestions will be VERY appreciated!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/umebottle3/fie_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||01-22-2001||07:25 PM||||Is the crack on the hood or the headlight door?  I am assuming the hood...<P>If the crack is seperating your going to need the strongest stuff you can find.  I have no idea which of those products is the best (little help?!?).  When you do fix it, you may want to put something on the back to reinfoce it.  Something like a piece of metal or even some fiberglass cloth.  Just to give it added strength so it doesn't come apart again.  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-22-2001||07:26 PM||||It may not be much cheaper to save it. Just how you fix it depends on the crack and where it is. It might just be easier to swap another hood than fix the crack. Either way you are likely to end up painting unless the replacement hood is the same color...<P>Main thing is if you can't get to the back side of the crack to reinforce the repair then it's very likely to crack again in future. Those door springs put a pretty good amount of load on the hood.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-23-2001||12:48 PM||||Im in body business and if its cracked it had some kind of stress sometime. A fix will just end up cracking again-find a good used hood so youll only have to paint it once. Im sure you can find one pretty cheap, lots of members here part out cars, you can find a whole car for less than $100.||||reg||1
